# Playwright conventions

**At a glance:** (1) role-first locators (2) web-first waits (3) POMs without asserts (4) storageState auth (5) unique self-cleaning data (6) one tag per `test()` (7) factories/enums/env (8) API for setup (9) mock edges not SUT (10) axe + keyboard (11) web-first asserts (12) isolation over retries.

## 1. Locators

Prefer locators that match how users and assistive tech find controls; reserve test ids for gaps only.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign in' }).click();
await page.getByLabel('Email').fill(process.env.APP_USER_EMAIL!);
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
await page.locator('#login-form > div:nth-child(2) button').click();
await page.locator('xpath=//button[contains(@class,"submit")]').click();
```

**Why:** Role and name track the accessible tree; CSS/XPath break on layout and styling changes.

## 2. Waiting

Let Playwright auto-wait via assertions and locators; never sleep or snapshot visibility into a variable before asserting.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Dashboard' })).toBeVisible();
await expect(page.getByText('Welcome back')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 10_000 });
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
await page.waitForTimeout(3000);
expect(await page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Dashboard' }).isVisible()).toBe(true);
```

**Why:** `expect(locator)` retries until the condition holds; timeouts and boolean snapshots race the UI.

## 3. Page Object Model

One class per page or component; expose locators from the constructor and methods that perform user actions only.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
export class SignInPage {
  constructor(private readonly page: Page) {}
  readonly email = this.page.getByLabel('Email');
  async signIn(email: string, password: string) {
    await this.email.fill(email);
    await this.page.getByLabel('Password').fill(password);
    await this.page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign in' }).click();
  }
}
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
async signInAndAssertDashboard() {
  await this.page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign in' }).click();
  await expect(this.page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Dashboard' })).toBeVisible();
}
```

**Why:** Specs own assertions; POMs stay reusable action layers.

## 4. Auth

Authenticate once per family in the setup project and reuse `storageState`; never repeat full login in each test.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
// auth.setup.ts — main family → AUTH_FILE, alt family → ALT_AUTH_FILE
test('two parents see the same invite', async ({ browser }) => {
  const alt = await browser.newContext({ storageState: ALT_AUTH_FILE });
  const altPage = await alt.newPage();
  // …
});
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
test('dashboard loads', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.getByLabel('Email').fill('parent@example.com');
  await page.getByLabel('Password').fill('hunter2');
});
```

**Why:** Setup project + `AUTH_FILE` / `ALT_AUTH_FILE` cuts flake and runtime; credentials belong in `process.env` only.

## 5. Test data

Generate unique data per test and tear it down; never rely on execution order or another student's rows in the shared environment.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
test('creates a playdate', async ({ request }) => {
  const title = `Playdate ${Date.now()}`;
  const id = await createPlaydateViaApi(request, { title });
  try {
    // … assert via UI
  } finally {
    await deletePlaydateViaApi(request, id);
  }
});
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
test('uses fixed playdate', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.getByText('Shared Demo Playdate').click(); // assumes prior test or manual seed
});
```

**Why:** Parallel runs and shared tenants need isolation; fixed titles collide across practicum accounts.

## 6. Tags

Put exactly one tag on each `test()`, never on `describe()`; reserve `@destructive` for shared global state and run those with `--workers=1`.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
test('sign in shows dashboard', { tag: '@smoke' }, async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/dashboard');
  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Dashboard' })).toBeVisible();
});
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
test.describe('Dashboard', { tag: '@smoke' }, () => {
  test('loads', async ({ page }) => { /* … */ });
});
```

**Why:** CI selects by tag on individual tests; `@destructive` serializes only true shared-state risk, not every mutating test that reverts in `afterEach`.

## 7. Test data sources

Centralize builders and enums; keep secrets and base URLs in env, not in specs.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
import { buildFamilyProfile } from '../test-data/factories/family';
import { AppRoute } from '../test-data/routes';

const user = buildFamilyProfile();
await page.goto(AppRoute.Dashboard);
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
await page.goto('https://example.test/app/dashboard');
await page.getByLabel('Child name').fill('FixedChildName');
```

**Why:** Factories + `routes.ts` keep data unique and strings consistent; env drives target URL per environment.

## 8. API

Use the `request` fixture to seed, tear down, and assert contracts; avoid slow UI-only setup when an API exists.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
test('lists created child', async ({ page, request }) => {
  const childId = await createChildViaApi(request, buildChild());
  await page.goto(`/children/${childId}`);
  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: /Child profile/i })).toBeVisible();
});
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
test('lists created child', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/children/new');
  // … ten UI steps to create prerequisite data
});
```

**Why:** API setup is faster, clearer, and easier to clean up than clicking through forms.

## 9. Network mocking

Stub dependency failures and edge payloads with `page.route`; never mock the endpoint the test is meant to verify.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
await page.route('**/api/notifications', (route) =>
  route.fulfill({ status: 503, body: '{}' }),
);
await page.goto('/dashboard');
await expect(page.getByText('Notifications unavailable')).toBeVisible();
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
await page.route('**/api/children', (route) =>
  route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ items: [] }) }),
);
// test title: "POST /api/children creates a child"
```

**Why:** Mock the edges you need for resilience tests; the system under test must hit the real handler.

## 10. Accessibility

Run axe on key flows and verify keyboard use; strong `getByRole({ name })` locators double as name checks.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
import AxeBuilder from '@axe-core/playwright';

test('sign-in page a11y', { tag: '@regression' }, async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/login');
  await expect(page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign in' })).toBeFocused();
  const results = await new AxeBuilder({ page }).withTags(['wcag2a', 'wcag2aa']).analyze();
  expect(results.violations).toEqual([]);
});
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
test('sign-in page', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/login');
  expect(await page.locator('.btn-primary').count()).toBeGreaterThan(0);
});
```

**Why:** WCAG scans catch systemic issues; role+name locators enforce accessible labels.

## 11. Assertions

Default to web-first `expect(locator)`; use `expect.soft` for grouped checks; screenshot only with masks for dynamic regions.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
await expect.soft(page.getByRole('alert')).toHaveText('Saved');
await expect(page.getByRole('status')).toBeVisible();
await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot('dashboard.png', {
  mask: [page.getByTestId('live-clock')],
});
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
const text = await page.locator('.toast').textContent();
expect(text).toContain('Saved');
await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot('dashboard.png'); // clock and avatars differ every run
```

**Why:** Locator assertions auto-wait; soft groups surface multiple failures; unmasked screenshots flake.

## 12. Anti-flake

Prefer isolation, clocks, and locale pins over cranking retries or workers; CI retries are a safety net, not a design.

✅ **Good**

```typescript
test.use({ locale: 'en-CA', timezoneId: 'America/Toronto' });

test('slot shows today', async ({ page, clock }) => {
  await clock.install({ time: new Date('2026-06-01T10:00:00-04:00') });
  await page.goto('/availability');
  await expect(page.getByRole('cell', { name: 'Mon, Jun 1' })).toBeVisible();
});
```

❌ **Bad**

```typescript
// playwright.config.ts — "make it pass"
retries: 5,
workers: 8, // for @destructive shared settings tests
```

**Why:** `page.clock` and config `locale`/`timezoneId` stabilize time; `@destructive` + `--workers=1` is intentional, not a default flake fix.

## Refusals (hard stops)

Never weaken or delete an assertion to pass; never heal a real bug; never replace a role locator with CSS/XPath; never use `waitForTimeout`, a hardcoded credential, or the `any` type. Each one is a conflict the agent raises, not a preference it can be talked out of.
